---
name: log-work
description: Record a Work log entry for this Claude Code session in today's Obsidian Daily note. Use only when the user runs /log-work.
disable-model-invocation: true
---

1. Write one sentence (English, no wikilinks) on what this session accomplished since its previous entry (an earlier `/log-work` or the automatic one at session end), or since the session started. Focus on the outcome, not the steps: start with a past-tense verb, at most 25 words, and mention PR and issue numbers when there are any.
2. Run, substituting the sentence:

   ```bash
   bash "${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/log-work.sh" "${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID}" "{{ .obsidianVault }}" "<sentence>"
   ```

   The script works out the active time windows (from the transcript) and the repository (from cwd), then writes the entry. Never edit the Daily note yourself, and don't commit in the vault.
3. Report the line it printed. If the vault wasn't reachable, it prints a block for the user to paste; show it verbatim.
